{"id":"cd370570e5548030","group":"58","path":"58/batch05/58-df-scalar-curvature.md","title":"Scalar Curvature","display":"df-scalar-curvature — Scalar Curvature","type":"definition","metadata":{"type":"definition","book":"Set Theory","book_abbrev":"58","label":"58-df-scalar-curvature","aliases":["58-df-scalar-curvature","Scalar Curvature"],"display":"df-scalar-curvature — Scalar Curvature","depends_on":["[[../batch20/58-df-ricci-curvature.md]]"]},"metadataError":null,"renderWarnings":[],"properties":[{"key":"type","html":"definition"},{"key":"book","html":"Set Theory"},{"key":"book_abbrev","html":"58"},{"key":"label","html":"58-df-scalar-curvature"},{"key":"aliases","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span>58-df-scalar-curvature</span><span>Scalar Curvature</span></div>"},{"key":"display","html":"df-scalar-curvature — Scalar Curvature"},{"key":"depends_on","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-1\" data-note=\"0b88ba4114f012c8\" href=\"?note=0b88ba4114f012c8\" title=\"../batch20/58-df-ricci-curvature.md\">../batch20/58-df-ricci-curvature.md</a></span></div>"}],"html":"\n<h2 id=\"Hypothesis\">[Hypothesis]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"s,\\rho,R,\\nabla,M,E,g,e,n\\in V\">\\(s,\\rho,R,\\nabla,M,E,g,e,n\\in V\\)</span></li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{RicciCurvature}_S:V^8\\to\\{\\top,\\bot\\}\">\\(\\mathrm{RicciCurvature}_S:V^8\\to\\{\\top,\\bot\\}\\)</span> (see <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-2\" data-note=\"0b88ba4114f012c8\" href=\"?note=0b88ba4114f012c8\" title=\"../batch20/58-df-ricci-curvature.md\">../batch20/58-df-ricci-curvature.md</a>)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{ScalarCurvature}_S:V^9\\to\\{\\top,\\bot\\}\">\\(\\mathrm{ScalarCurvature}_S:V^9\\to\\{\\top,\\bot\\}\\)</span></li>\n</ul>\n<h2 id=\"Assertion\">[Assertion]</h2>\n<figure class=\"equation\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{df\\text{-}scalar\\text{-}curvature}\\vdash\\mathrm{ScalarCurvature}_S(s,\\rho,R,\\nabla,M,E,g,e,n)\\leftrightarrow\\mathrm{RicciCurvature}_S(\\rho;R,\\nabla,M,E,g,e,n)\\land s\\in\\mathbb R\\land s=\\sum_{i\\in n}\\rho(\\langle e(i),e(i)\\rangle)\"><div class=\"math-display\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"数学公式\">\\[\\mathrm{df\\text{-}scalar\\text{-}curvature}\\vdash\\mathrm{ScalarCurvature}_S(s,\\rho,R,\\nabla,M,E,g,e,n)\\leftrightarrow\\mathrm{RicciCurvature}_S(\\rho;R,\\nabla,M,E,g,e,n)\\land s\\in\\mathbb R\\land s=\\sum_{i\\in n}\\rho(\\langle e(i),e(i)\\rangle)\\]</div><button class=\"equation-action\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"展开查看完整公式\">展开公式 ↗</button></figure><h2 id=\"Remark\">[Remark]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>Scalar curvature is the trace of Ricci.  In the present library encoding, <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"E\">\\(E\\)</span>, <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"g\">\\(g\\)</span>, and <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"e\">\\(e\\)</span> describe one metric tangent carrier and an orthonormal basis code, so this atom defines the corresponding scalar value rather than postulating an unsupported global Ricci-field selector <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\operatorname{Ric}_g(p)\">\\(\\operatorname{Ric}_g(p)\\)</span>.</li>\n<li>For an Einstein metric <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\operatorname{Ric}_g=\\lambda g\">\\(\\operatorname{Ric}_g=\\lambda g\\)</span>, scalar curvature satisfies <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"R=n\\lambda\">\\(R=n\\lambda\\)</span>.</li>\n<li>The sign of <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"s(p)\">\\(s(p)\\)</span> controls the leading scalar-curvature correction to the volume of sufficiently small geodesic balls at <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"p\">\\(p\\)</span>.</li>\n<li>Round spheres have positive scalar curvature; flat tori have zero scalar curvature, and tori admit no metric of everywhere positive scalar curvature.</li>\n<li>Einstein: <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"R = \\lambda n\">\\(R = \\lambda n\\)</span> for Einstein metric; uniqueness for some manifolds</li>\n</ul>\n<h2 id=\"Reference\">[Reference]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>Besse, Einstein Manifolds</li>\n<li>do Carmo, Riemannian Geometry</li>\n</ul>\n","headings":[{"id":"Hypothesis","text":"[Hypothesis]","level":2},{"id":"Assertion","text":"[Assertion]","level":2},{"id":"Remark","text":"[Remark]","level":2},{"id":"Reference","text":"[Reference]","level":2}],"links":[{"target":"../batch20/58-df-ricci-curvature.md","status":"resolved","id":"0b88ba4114f012c8","anchor":"ref-1","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[../batch20/58-df-ricci-curvature.md]]","embed":false},{"target":"../batch20/58-df-ricci-curvature.md","status":"resolved","id":"0b88ba4114f012c8","anchor":"ref-2","targetAnchor":"","location":"正文","heading":"[Hypothesis]","excerpt":"$\\mathrm{RicciCurvature}_S:V^8\\to\\{\\top,\\bot\\}$ (see [[../batch20/58-df-ricci-curvature.md]])","embed":false}],"math":[{"tex":"s,\\rho,R,\\nabla,M,E,g,e,n\\in V","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{RicciCurvature}_S:V^8\\to\\{\\top,\\bot\\}","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{ScalarCurvature}_S:V^9\\to\\{\\top,\\bot\\}","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{df\\text{-}scalar\\text{-}curvature}\\vdash\\mathrm{ScalarCurvature}_S(s,\\rho,R,\\nabla,M,E,g,e,n)\\leftrightarrow\\mathrm{RicciCurvature}_S(\\rho;R,\\nabla,M,E,g,e,n)\\land s\\in\\mathbb R\\land s=\\sum_{i\\in n}\\rho(\\langle e(i),e(i)\\rangle)","display":true},{"tex":"E","display":false},{"tex":"g","display":false},{"tex":"e","display":false},{"tex":"\\operatorname{Ric}_g(p)","display":false},{"tex":"\\operatorname{Ric}_g=\\lambda g","display":false},{"tex":"R=n\\lambda","display":false},{"tex":"s(p)","display":false},{"tex":"p","display":false},{"tex":"R = \\lambda n","display":false}],"bytes":1644,"backlinks":[{"id":"84daad544872cc71","anchor":"ref-1116","locations":["正文"],"count":1,"excerpt":"[[../batch05/58-df-scalar-curvature.md|58-df-scalar-curvature]]（batch05）"}],"outgoing":["0b88ba4114f012c8"]}